{
 "_source": "data/runs/R-002 (run.json ctx, spec), data/evidence/R-002/ledger.jsonl and data/demo-repo diff 95a3488..8a8f29c, copied 2026-10-14; absolute paths dropped",
 "run": "R-002",
 "intent": "Let format() handle currencies without cents, like JPY: format(1235, \"JPY\") should give \"¥1,235\", and existing USD output must stay the same.",
 "title": "Format zero-decimal currencies",
 "createdAt": "2026-10-14T09:26:26.235Z",
 "spec": {
  "title": "format() supports JPY, a currency without cents",
  "what": "format() takes an optional currency code as a second argument. With \"JPY\" the amount counts whole yen, with no decimal part: the output is the ¥ sign followed by the amount with commas between thousands, and a leading minus sign for negative amounts (format(1235, \"JPY\") is \"¥1,235\", format(-1235, \"JPY\") is \"-¥1,235\", format(0, \"JPY\") is \"¥0\"). With no currency, or with \"USD\", the output stays exactly as it is on base, with no thousands separators added (format(123456) stays \"$1234.56\").",
  "why": [
   "Some currencies, like the Japanese yen, have no minor unit. format() assumes cents everywhere, so 1235 yen comes out as \"$12.35\": the wrong symbol and the wrong value.",
   "Existing callers pass only an amount and depend on today's USD text, so the default output has to stay the same.",
   "The captain's example \"¥1,235\" has a thousands separator while USD output has none today. This spec adds grouping for JPY only and leaves USD unchanged, as the intent says."
  ],
  "done": [
   "test/format.test.ts: format(1235, \"JPY\") returns \"¥1,235\"; fails on base, where format ignores the currency and returns \"$12.35\".",
   "test/format.test.ts: format(-1235, \"JPY\") returns \"-¥1,235\" and format(0, \"JPY\") returns \"¥0\"; fails on base, where the calls return \"-$12.35\" and \"$0.00\".",
   "test/format.test.ts: in one test, format(123456, \"JPY\") returns \"¥123,456\" while format(123456) and format(123456, \"USD\") both return \"$1234.56\" (no separator added to USD); fails on base, where the JPY call returns \"$1234.56\".",
   "test/format.test.ts: in one test, format(1999, \"JPY\") returns \"¥1,999\" while format(1999, \"USD\") returns \"$19.99\", the same text as format(1999); fails on base, where the JPY call returns \"$19.99\". The three existing USD tests in test/format.test.ts and all tests in test/money.test.ts keep passing unchanged."
  ],
  "scope": [
   "src/money.ts",
   "test/format.test.ts",
   "test/money.test.ts",
   "README.md"
  ],
  "door": {
   "kind": "two-way",
   "reason": "An optional parameter added to one library function; no sensitive paths (.github, CODEOWNERS, gates) are touched and the default behaviour stays the same, so it is easy to revert."
  },
  "explain": {
   "en": "Today format() treats every amount as US cents, so 1235 yen comes out as \"$12.35\". After this change you can pass a currency: format(1235, \"JPY\") gives \"¥1,235\", with commas between thousands and no decimals. Calling format() without a currency, or with \"USD\", gives the same text as before.",
   "zh-TW": "目前 format() 把每個金額都當成美分，所以 1235 日圓會顯示成「$12.35」。改動之後可以傳入幣別：format(1235, \"JPY\") 會得到「¥1,235」，千位有逗號、沒有小數。不傳幣別或傳 \"USD\" 時，輸出和以前完全一樣。"
  },
  "version": 2
 },
